This happened to me recently (the other way around). I dropped from
mines level 4 (with pet) to Mine Town (level 5, without pet). The Town
was the level with the two trees and the statue of the Gnome King, and
the priest at the top middle.

I arrived in the room with the downstairs, so it promised to be a long
trip to the upstairs at the top left. To make things worse, a wererat
appeared in the door and summoned three of his brethren.

What appeared to be extremely useful was that I could still pray, had my
full 25 HP, one reserved potion of healing, and my still charged wand of
sleep. By very careful use of that wand, I could sleep all adversaries
and *still* keep an open route through the room to the door.

Once I was out in the open, I managed to make my way to the upstairs,
and pay a visit to the priest first. I did become level two before I got
there, though, but the shopkeepers I had visited earlier in the main
dungeon had raised my zorkmid level to approximately 4200, and the first
gift to the priest yielded 4 points of AC, so I still gained 8 points
total, almost the maximum 9 points.

Once I had talked to the priest, I couldn't care less about pacifism any
longer, but I still remained careful while going back up to my pet.

That character didn't last, though. It appeared the wererat had gotten a
bite in, and I was afflicted with lycanthropy. I prayed too soon, and
changing back and forth eventually did me in (you have to drop almost
*everything* when in rat form).

